From a0c05f0da7f6e0e7f1ea8882c04c315e42d7944b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:33:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kk: One MTL4CommandBuffer per VkCommandBuffer

Origin:      https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43697
             branch kk-encoding-rework, upstream commit a0c05f0da7f
Author:      Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>, not ours. Do not re-author.
Status:      candidate, NOT APPLIED
Applies-to:  mesa 73a03c611018d842bf3da0b5c3084a5f949540e8 (its own merge base)
             Does NOT apply to our pin 56588ef0665: that predates Metal 4
             encoding, so there is nothing here to fix.
Expires:     when the MR merges upstream, or is abandoned
Evidence:    fixes issue 15998. Control 73a03c61101 dies at the 20 GiB ceiling
             in 43s. With this, engine peak holds flat at 11-12 GiB for 120s.
             coding-agents/MACOS_PERFORMANCE.md, "Mesa pin and issue 15998"
Note:        staged so the leak fix does not depend on an unmerged MR branch
             surviving on GitLab. Needed only when the pin moves past Metal 4.

Removes pre and post graphics approach with a streamlined command buffer.
The downside is that unroll, tessellation and any compute work required
mid render will split the render pass. Writes are correctly pushed to the
render pass end. Long term, we need to move unroll and tessellation to
mesh shader, and indirect draw count to a vertex dispatch that encodes
the ICB for the draw. This change also allows for simplification of
synchronization to allow overlap.

We don't need to call reset on the allocators since command buffers will
return the allocator memory on completion

Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
